This product builds on and includes third-party work:

- SAM 2 / SAM 2.1 (Meta Platforms, Inc.), Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2
  Used as a library and as the teacher model. The released sam2-lite models contain SAM 2.1
  weights (memory encoder, mask decoder and a fine-tuned memory attention).

- src/sam2lite/eval/third_party/sav_benchmark.py: SAM 2's J&F evaluator, vendored unmodified,
  with its licenses in the same folder:
    BSD License, SAM 2 Eval software (Meta Platforms, Inc.)
    BSD 3-Clause License, DAVIS: Densely Annotated VIdeo Segmentation (davis2017-evaluation)
    MIT License, Rex Cheng (vos-benchmark)

- timm (PyTorch Image Models), Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
  Provides the MobileNetV4 backbone and its pretrained weights. The weights are tagged Apache 2.0
  but were trained on ImageNet-1k, whose terms of access allow only non-commercial research and
  educational use (https://image-net.org/download.php).

- DAVIS 2017 dataset (Pont-Tuset et al., 2017; Perazzi et al., 2016), Creative Commons
  Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 (CC BY-NC 4.0), as stated in the README of the official
  dataset package. https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/
  Some sequences come from third-party online sources with their own terms of use (listed in
  the package's SOURCES.md). The models were distilled on DAVIS 2017 train frames and evaluated
  on DAVIS 2017 val. No DAVIS videos, frames or annotations are redistributed.

Because of the ImageNet and DAVIS terms above, the released sam2-lite models are for
non-commercial research use only.
